    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 2026-04-13; see the referring visit&apos;s Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Thin, alert, and quick</td></tr><tr><td>Abdomen</td><td>Soft and non-tender; bladder not palpable with the catheter draining</td></tr><tr><td>Genitourinary</td><td>Normal external genitalia; catheter draining light pink urine; meatus clean</td></tr><tr><td>Rectal</td><td>Prostate enlarged, about 70 to 80 mL, firm and smooth, with no discrete nodule; no fixed pelvic mass felt</td></tr><tr><td>Cystoscopy</td><td>Flexible cystoscopy: trilobar prostatic enlargement with friable surface vessels; a solid, sessile, partly necrotic tumor about 4 cm on the posterior wall extending to the dome, with surrounding white keratinizing plaques; no other lesions; ureteric orifices clear. Catheter replaced</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
